    "notes": [
        "Encodes the rules that were hard-coded in harAnalyzer.js before country support was added; behaviour must stay identical.",
        "enforcement.accepted is the short DIGG URL: it counts as a correct link but produces no info issue, exactly as before.",
        "Date triggers: the date whose trigger has the LOWEST weight is reported as the updated date (legacy behaviour), so 'uppdater' (0.5) beats 'bedömning' (1.0).",
        "letters keeps the A-ZÅÄÖ character classes the old code used to cut out the sentence around a match; other countries use Unicode letter classes.",
        "Two regex typos from the old code were fixed when moving to Unicode mode: a stray ']' after 'test(ning|er){0,1}' and a space inside '{1, 6}' in the self-assessment pattern.",
        "'.nu' and '.stockholm' are treated as Swedish: .nu is used almost only by Swedish sites, and .stockholm is the City of Stockholm's TLD."
    ]
